  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are lots of action nodes which require a predefined type of Component of their input and it becomes tiringly and space-inefficient to manually add lots of \"GameObject.GetComponent\"+\"Type\" nodes to provide the needed input for the node. So, it would be really useful if Udon could \"auto-get-component\" (auto-cast) inputs if the type of Component is explicitly defined for an input. This would also be highly useful when making changes to \"self\" object (\"self\" is by default in all \"instance\" inputs), but since we still need to provide an exact component, we still need to add \"GetComponent+Type\" nodes even for \"self-management\". See the example image: red circles are just \"self-get-component\" which won't be necessary in case of auto-casting. Greens are redundant GetComponent of another variable.\nAs a side-addition, it would be nice if such noodles would be somehow highlighted so that the developer could clearly see that a \"type-cast\" is attempted here.",
